 ## Background
-The Clustered Grid Cell data structure was proposed in a paper by [S1] to address the limitations of existing isosurface rendering methods that require extracting another representation of the data or relying on the original volume data during rendering. It builds on the concept of cell rasterization using billboard splatting, as introduced in previous work [13] (referenced in [S1]), but improves upon it by storing corner scalar values with each cell and organizing them into a clustered hierarchy for efficient culling and rendering. The method supports visibility buffer culling and EWA-based interpolation of attributes like normals [S1].
